WEBVTT

00:01.865 --> 00:03.166
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:03.168 --> 00:05.719
So, Marty, uh,
what are we celebrating?

00:05.721 --> 00:07.554
My prostate exam.

00:08.372 --> 00:11.207
Doctor gave me a thumbs up.

00:11.209 --> 00:13.543
At least it felt like a thumb.

00:13.545 --> 00:15.395
Well, I'm glad to hear
you're in good health.

00:15.397 --> 00:18.548
Yes, he said I could live
another ten years

00:18.550 --> 00:20.066
if I give up alcohol.

00:20.068 --> 00:21.634
Yeah, but you're
drinking Scotch.

00:21.636 --> 00:23.253
He had a finger up my keister.

00:23.255 --> 00:24.604
What, am I gonna argue?

00:26.407 --> 00:28.108
It's true; he never complains
when I put my...

00:28.110 --> 00:29.392
(watch beeping)

00:29.394 --> 00:32.328
What is that, the horrifying
conversation alarm?

00:32.330 --> 00:33.563
(beeping continues)

00:33.565 --> 00:36.983
I was hoping it was a truck
about to back over me.

00:36.985 --> 00:38.585
It's time for my pills.

00:38.587 --> 00:40.587
Evy, I think I left them
in the car.

00:40.589 --> 00:42.172
Would you get them?
Of course, dear.

00:42.174 --> 00:44.257
I think the keys are
in my pocket.

00:44.259 --> 00:46.443
You may have to root
around for them.

00:46.445 --> 00:48.128
Really nice try.

00:48.130 --> 00:49.379
I-I got to remember that.

00:49.381 --> 00:50.847
That's a good one.

00:50.849 --> 00:54.651
You actually have
to own something to have keys.

00:54.653 --> 00:58.505
Okay, let me tell you
why I'm really here.

00:58.507 --> 01:01.591
You know I have been dating
your mother for some time now.

01:01.593 --> 01:02.925
Uh, actually,
she's not my mom.

01:02.927 --> 01:04.811
Yeah, or mine.

01:04.813 --> 01:07.063
Well, you boys are a couple
and she's your daughter,

01:07.065 --> 01:08.782
so we're like family.

01:08.784 --> 01:11.151
Oh.

01:11.153 --> 01:13.369
No, we're-we're not married.

01:13.371 --> 01:14.954
Oh, but someday.

01:14.956 --> 01:17.940
No, no, we-we don't want
to get married.

01:17.942 --> 01:20.577
So why did you guys fight
so hard for it?

01:20.579 --> 01:23.129
Yeah, come on, Walden.

01:23.131 --> 01:26.316
You're here, you're queer,
get used to it.

01:26.318 --> 01:27.834
As I was saying,

01:27.836 --> 01:32.088
your mother is a beautiful,
warm, compassionate woman.

01:32.090 --> 01:34.474
Everyone's entitled
to their opinion.

01:34.476 --> 01:37.677
I would like to ask
for her hand in marriage.

01:37.679 --> 01:39.529
Aw. Wow.
What?

01:39.531 --> 01:41.347
So, what do you say?

01:41.349 --> 01:43.650
Can I make an honest woman
out of your mother?

01:43.652 --> 01:46.135
I doubt it.

01:47.638 --> 01:49.856
But you have my blessing.

01:49.858 --> 01:51.441
Mine, too.
Congratulations.

01:51.443 --> 01:52.942
Uh, wait, not-not so fast.

01:52.944 --> 01:54.143
I have a question first.

01:54.145 --> 01:56.863
Would you allow her son
to come and live with you

01:56.865 --> 01:58.915
if his current living
quarters were to, say,

01:58.917 --> 02:00.817
suddenly become a sauna?

02:01.886 --> 02:03.620
Any son of Evelyn's

02:03.622 --> 02:06.489
always has a place in my home.

02:06.491 --> 02:08.842
Welcome to the family, Dad.

02:08.844 --> 02:10.677
(door opens)

02:10.679 --> 02:12.212
Here are your pills, dear.

02:12.214 --> 02:15.598
Look at that, a hot chick
carrying a bag of drugs.

02:15.600 --> 02:19.502
It's like 1970 all over again.

02:20.621 --> 02:22.505
Let's start
with the muscle relaxers.

02:22.507 --> 02:24.757
One for you, two for me.

02:25.659 --> 02:27.844
Wow. What are
all those for?

02:27.846 --> 02:29.279
It's a combination.

02:29.281 --> 02:31.064
Hardeners and softeners.

02:31.066 --> 02:33.566
I-I have to take these or...

02:33.568 --> 02:35.568
(grunting)

02:36.537 --> 02:38.037
Marty, are you okay?
Quick, quick.

02:38.039 --> 02:40.623
P-Press the medic alert.

02:41.458 --> 02:43.960
What is this?

02:43.962 --> 02:45.378
This is a ring.

02:46.697 --> 02:50.733
I've fallen for you,
and I can't get up.

02:50.735 --> 02:51.918
What are you saying?

02:51.920 --> 02:53.253
Will you marry me?

02:53.255 --> 02:55.672
I can't believe this.

02:55.674 --> 02:57.757
You are so romantic.

02:57.759 --> 02:59.375
Will I have to sign a prenup?

02:59.377 --> 03:00.410
Of course not.

03:00.412 --> 03:02.378
Then yes,

03:02.380 --> 03:05.231
And I want your son
to be my best man.

03:05.233 --> 03:06.683
Oh, my God, really?

03:06.685 --> 03:09.319
Not you; pretty boy over there.

03:10.721 --> 03:12.188
Oh.

03:12.190 --> 03:14.390
In my heart, I knew.

03:16.076 --> 03:17.744
Okay, but at the ceremony,

03:17.746 --> 03:20.413
I'm not gonna root around
in your pocket for the ring.

03:20.415 --> 03:22.832
And, Jennifer,
you'll be my maid of honor?

03:22.834 --> 03:25.585
(scoffs) Of course.
It's like I'm not even here.

03:25.587 --> 03:27.704
Sweet.
I love straight weddings.

03:27.706 --> 03:30.173
A bunch
of drunk bridesmaids crying

03:30.175 --> 03:31.541
because they don't have a man.

03:31.543 --> 03:34.410
It's like eating fish
in a barrel.

03:34.412 --> 03:36.546
So, where are we gonna have
the ceremony?

03:36.548 --> 03:38.715
Why don't we just have
it here at our place?

03:38.717 --> 03:40.750
Uh, maybe &lt;i>we&lt;/i> should
discuss this

03:40.752 --> 03:43.269
before &lt;i>we&lt;/i> offer up &lt;i>our&lt;/i> place.

03:43.271 --> 03:45.388
Do what I do;
just go along with it,

03:45.390 --> 03:48.308
and later, take it out on him
in the bedroom.

03:49.827 --> 03:52.312
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:52.314 --> 03:53.561
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.

03:53.562 --> 03:57.562
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x13 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">Bite Me, Supreme Court&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on January 30, 2014

03:57.563 --> 04:02.563
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

04:02.589 --> 04:03.839
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

04:03.889 --> 04:05.186
Oh, Berta, uh,

04:05.187 --> 04:06.324
can I try something out on you?

04:06.341 --> 04:08.975
There isn't enough
alcohol in the world.

04:09.177 --> 04:11.611
No, I'm writing a toast
for my mother's wedding.

04:11.613 --> 04:12.829
Uh, so far I've got, uh,

04:12.831 --> 04:14.464
"Ladies and gentlemen,
I am so pleased

04:14.466 --> 04:16.099
"to welcome Marty Pepper
to our family.

04:16.101 --> 04:17.884
"Uh, to know Marty
is to love him.

04:17.886 --> 04:20.019
"He's a kind,
sweet and generous man,

04:20.021 --> 04:21.254
"which proves once and for all

04:21.256 --> 04:23.506
that opposites
really do attract."

04:23.508 --> 04:26.726
So, you're telling everyone
you're a son of a bitch.

04:27.711 --> 04:29.095
I like it.

04:30.381 --> 04:31.931
Hey, Alan, I need your help

04:31.933 --> 04:33.983
planning this geriatric
bachelor party.

04:33.985 --> 04:35.568
I started reaching out
to the guys

04:35.570 --> 04:36.769
on Marty's invite list,

04:36.771 --> 04:41.057
and so far I got dead,
dead, coma, Florida.

04:41.059 --> 04:44.027
Hey, uh, where you thinking
about having this thing anyway?

04:44.029 --> 04:45.478
Well, at this point, either Boca

04:45.480 --> 04:48.264
or the
Hollywood Forever Cemetery.

04:48.266 --> 04:49.782
How about a strip club?

04:49.784 --> 04:51.751
I know a place with a great
all-you-can-eat buffet.

04:51.753 --> 04:53.316
Two things you never
want to hear together.

04:53.317 --> 04:55.311
- Mm-hmm.
- "Strip club" and "all-you-can-eat""

04:55.373 --> 04:57.790
Besides, Marty doesn't
want strippers.

04:57.792 --> 04:59.459
You can't have a bachelor party
without strippers.

04:59.461 --> 05:00.743
But more importantly,

05:00.745 --> 05:02.629
we can't let the last
naked woman this man sees

05:02.631 --> 05:03.913
be my mother.

05:05.216 --> 05:08.301
My granddaughters do
a great two-for-one show.

05:08.303 --> 05:09.953
I can get you a family discount.

05:09.955 --> 05:12.088
No, no.

05:12.090 --> 05:13.289
We... No strippers.

05:13.291 --> 05:15.391
We're just doing
a nice steak dinner.

05:15.393 --> 05:16.726
Well, if there's not
gonna be any strippers,

05:16.728 --> 05:17.727
then I'm not going.

05:17.729 --> 05:19.428
Actually,
you're not on the list.

05:19.430 --> 05:21.597
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

05:21.599 --> 05:23.399
Okay, okay,
one more time.

05:23.401 --> 05:26.936
I want a nice filet,
medium-rare,

05:26.938 --> 05:28.955
and then you give
it a nice sear,

05:28.957 --> 05:31.958
and then you put it
in the food processor,

05:31.960 --> 05:33.442
and you give it a pump

05:33.444 --> 05:35.611
three times on chop--
boom, boom, boom--

05:35.613 --> 05:37.964
and two times on
dice-- boom, boom.

05:37.966 --> 05:39.999
Thank you.

05:40.884 --> 05:42.502
Oh, uh,

05:42.504 --> 05:44.120
is, uh, this the party

05:44.122 --> 05:45.655
or the bathroom?

05:45.657 --> 05:47.423
Here. Over here, Tim.

05:47.425 --> 05:48.675
Oh.
Yeah.

05:48.677 --> 05:50.209
Thank you.

05:50.211 --> 05:51.311
What's with the glasses?

05:51.313 --> 05:52.879
You look like Bono.

05:52.881 --> 05:55.181
I was fortunate enough
to work with Bono.

05:55.183 --> 05:58.818
Yeah, and, uh, at the time,
he was married to Cher.

05:59.937 --> 06:02.071
I just got back
from the eye doctor.

06:02.073 --> 06:04.907
Boy, he robbed me blind.

06:04.909 --> 06:08.328
can only read the top
line of the eye chart.

06:08.330 --> 06:10.163
It says P.

06:10.165 --> 06:12.915
Then I have to.

06:12.917 --> 06:15.652
I-I'd like to, uh,
to propose a toast.

06:15.654 --> 06:17.036
Uh, first to Walden

06:17.038 --> 06:19.122
for putting all this together
at the last minute.

06:19.124 --> 06:21.507
Well, it was tough,
but I managed to get a table

06:21.509 --> 06:24.210
at 3:00 p.m. on a Thursday.

06:24.212 --> 06:27.547
To Walden and his wife Alan.

06:29.433 --> 06:31.634
That is one ugly woman.

06:31.636 --> 06:32.668
Uh-huh.

06:32.670 --> 06:35.138
Um, my, uh,

06:35.140 --> 06:37.473
my mother and I have
had our ups and downs,

06:37.475 --> 06:40.360
but I love her,
and I want her to be happy.

06:40.362 --> 06:42.445
And you, Marty Pepper,

06:42.447 --> 06:44.347
make her happy,
which means

06:44.349 --> 06:45.848
I love you.

06:47.051 --> 06:49.952
I thought we
said no broads.

06:51.205 --> 06:53.489
I had a gay friend
who was arrested for sodomy,

06:53.491 --> 06:57.694
and he had the charge reduced
to following too closely.

06:57.696 --> 06:59.629
Uh, anyway,

06:59.631 --> 07:03.049
um, I want to wish you both
the best. Cheers.

07:03.051 --> 07:04.384
Tim needs a drink.

07:04.386 --> 07:07.920
No, no, no, no, uh, I'm driving.

07:07.922 --> 07:10.039
Marty, last time I saw you,

07:10.041 --> 07:14.210
we were in a threesome
with that cute little redhead.

07:14.212 --> 07:16.145
What ever happened to her?

07:16.147 --> 07:17.513
I'm marrying her.

07:17.515 --> 07:19.215
Nice girl.

07:19.217 --> 07:21.100
Hard worker.

07:22.603 --> 07:25.721
Well, I'd like to say on behalf
of all of us, getting married?

07:25.723 --> 07:27.940
What the hell are
you doing, Marty?

07:27.942 --> 07:29.725
Why do you need
seven wives?

07:29.727 --> 07:33.363
You can barely get through
nine holes of golf!

07:33.365 --> 07:37.166
She's a sweet kid,
and I need a little warmth

07:37.168 --> 07:39.619
and comfort
at the end of the day.

07:39.621 --> 07:43.222
Have you ever considered
a nice piece of toast?

07:44.425 --> 07:46.959
(clears throat) Uh, well,
I would like to say something.

07:46.961 --> 07:50.246
Uh... I might be
in the minority here,

07:50.248 --> 07:52.515
but I still believe in love,

07:52.517 --> 07:54.717
and it's inspiring to know

07:54.719 --> 07:58.020
that even at your age,
you can still find it.

07:58.022 --> 08:00.139
Now we have two broads.

08:01.608 --> 08:03.226
The kid is right.

08:03.228 --> 08:06.595
Nothing is more important
than love,

08:06.597 --> 08:09.198
except a good opening weekend.

08:09.200 --> 08:11.818
And salt.

08:12.953 --> 08:15.988
Damn it, I really miss salt.

08:15.990 --> 08:18.624
Okay, we're here because
we love this man.

08:18.626 --> 08:21.394
You know, not the way
you two love each other.

08:21.396 --> 08:23.396
But...

08:23.398 --> 08:25.781
love, n-nonetheless.

08:27.551 --> 08:30.586
We're also here for the free
steak, am I right? (chuckles)

08:30.588 --> 08:33.639
Excuse me.

08:33.641 --> 08:35.041
Who is this kid?

08:35.043 --> 08:37.059
He's Evelyn's son.

08:37.061 --> 08:39.095
Who's Evelyn?

08:39.097 --> 08:40.563
The woman I'm marrying.

08:40.565 --> 08:42.298
You're getting married?

08:42.300 --> 08:45.301
Mazel tov!

08:47.404 --> 08:49.822
Which one of you guys
is... Marty?

08:53.510 --> 08:54.911
I'm Sugar.

08:54.913 --> 08:55.778
I'm Cinnamon.

08:55.780 --> 08:58.531
I'm rich!
I'm richer!

08:58.533 --> 09:00.750
Hey, I thought we said
no strippers.

09:00.752 --> 09:02.201
It's a bachelor party;
loosen up.

09:02.203 --> 09:03.819
Hey, uh, Marty,
you up for a lap dance?

09:03.821 --> 09:06.422
I haven't been up
for a lap dance

09:06.424 --> 09:09.375
since the
Reagan Administration.

09:09.377 --> 09:11.360
Governor Reagan's.

09:11.362 --> 09:13.880
I think I wrote that joke.

09:13.882 --> 09:16.415
Girls, give him something
to remember.

09:16.417 --> 09:18.601
Uh, they're the green ones.

09:19.436 --> 09:20.987
Oh, uh, and don't forget,

09:20.989 --> 09:22.805
I'm only paying for an hour,
so whether you're

09:22.807 --> 09:24.507
in the middle
of a lap dance or CPR,

09:24.509 --> 09:25.892
you got to get out of there.

09:28.028 --> 09:30.179
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

09:30.181 --> 09:32.698
I want to find something
Marty will like.

09:32.700 --> 09:36.219
I wonder if they have
edible underwear for diabetics.

09:36.221 --> 09:37.520
Well, they do have
something called

09:37.522 --> 09:39.522
"I Can't Believe
It's Not Body Butter."

09:39.524 --> 09:42.358
(chuckles)
Hey, you'd look good in these.

09:42.360 --> 09:45.027
No, dear,
Marty would look good in them.

09:45.029 --> 09:47.797
Oh, you guys &lt;i>are&lt;/i> kinky.

09:47.799 --> 09:51.250
If we got any kinkier, we'd
upset the animal rights people.

09:54.304 --> 09:56.839
So, how about
you, Jennifer?

09:56.841 --> 09:58.808
Are there wedding
bells in your future?

09:58.810 --> 09:59.926
It is legal now.

09:59.928 --> 10:01.260
Oh, don't remind me.

10:01.262 --> 10:04.230
I used to have the perfect get-
out-of-relationship-free card.

10:04.232 --> 10:06.816
"Oh, I'd love to marry you,

10:06.818 --> 10:09.986
"but darn all that prejudice
and intolerance.

10:09.988 --> 10:12.738
Bite me, Supreme Court."

10:12.740 --> 10:14.040
Well, you never know.

10:14.042 --> 10:15.875
I didn't expect to find
love this late in life,

10:15.877 --> 10:18.110
but there's just something
about Marty.

10:18.112 --> 10:22.114
Yeah, there's just
400 million things about Marty.

10:22.116 --> 10:23.533
Yes, but I would love him

10:23.535 --> 10:25.985
if he was only
worth 200 million.

10:25.987 --> 10:27.086
(laughs)

10:27.088 --> 10:29.572
You know,
I was really touched

10:29.574 --> 10:31.674
when you asked me to be
your maid of honor.

10:31.676 --> 10:33.826
Well, you're the
daughter of my only son.

10:33.828 --> 10:34.927
Well, what about Alan?

10:34.929 --> 10:36.879
Don't spoil my day, dear.

10:36.881 --> 10:38.965
And having you
with me is like

10:38.967 --> 10:40.716
having Charlie around.

10:40.718 --> 10:43.269
This will be the only one of
my weddings without him.

10:43.271 --> 10:44.937
Well, except the first one,
of course.

10:44.939 --> 10:47.607
Oh, no, dear,
he was there.

10:47.609 --> 10:50.226
It was the first time
we got drunk together.

10:50.228 --> 10:52.428
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:52.430 --> 10:54.280
Where's Marty?

10:54.282 --> 10:56.232
Nobody likes a stripper hog.

10:56.234 --> 10:58.000
Oh, speaking of hogs,

10:58.002 --> 11:00.319
I once did a show
with Miss Piggy.

11:00.321 --> 11:03.122
You know there's a
guy under there?

11:03.124 --> 11:05.875
You know, maybe we should go
check on him.

11:05.877 --> 11:07.109
MARTY:
I'm fine!

11:07.111 --> 11:10.830
Best present that I ever had
in my whole life.

11:10.832 --> 11:12.632
Thank you, Walden.

11:12.634 --> 11:14.617
Actually, the strippers
were my idea. (chuckles)

11:14.619 --> 11:16.252
Oh, well,
then you tell your mother

11:16.254 --> 11:17.670
the wedding is off.

11:17.672 --> 11:21.290
Tell her what?

11:21.292 --> 11:22.725
STEVE:
Okay.

11:22.727 --> 11:23.993
Wedding pool.

11:23.995 --> 11:25.011
I have

11:25.013 --> 11:26.462
"Misplaces teeth

11:26.464 --> 11:28.464
and can't recite the vows."

11:28.466 --> 11:29.615
Uh-huh.

11:30.684 --> 11:33.819
I had, uh... (clears throat)

11:33.821 --> 11:37.523
"Died during the lap dance."

11:38.975 --> 11:42.411
I had "This man's
name is Gary.

11:42.413 --> 11:44.013
"If found,

11:44.015 --> 11:47.667
"take him to 104
North Beverly Drive.

11:47.669 --> 11:50.870
Do not give him Scotch""

11:52.005 --> 11:53.422
Well, I have... (clears throat)

11:53.424 --> 11:55.424
"Alan will
screw this up somehow."

11:55.426 --> 11:56.876
I win.

11:56.878 --> 11:58.010
Are you serious?

11:58.012 --> 11:59.378
You can't call off the wedding.

11:59.380 --> 12:00.680
You're not thinking clearly.

12:00.682 --> 12:03.883
I have never been more clear
about anything in my life,

12:03.885 --> 12:06.268
except casting Ralph Macchio.

12:06.270 --> 12:08.688
Kid was a born star.

12:08.690 --> 12:11.507
Well, I think the party is over.

12:11.509 --> 12:15.027
Can somebody please drive me
to, uh,

12:15.029 --> 12:18.948
104 North Beverly Drive?

12:18.950 --> 12:20.683
I gotcha.

12:20.685 --> 12:25.021
Listen, maybe on the way home,
we can pick up some Scotch.

12:25.023 --> 12:27.039
Wait, wait, not so fast!

12:27.041 --> 12:28.841
I got a catheter.

12:28.843 --> 12:30.710
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:37.115 --> 12:38.432
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

12:38.434 --> 12:40.283
I can't believe Marty
called off the wedding.

12:40.285 --> 12:42.569
I can't believe
I left a bachelor party

12:42.571 --> 12:44.888
at 4:45 in the afternoon.

12:44.890 --> 12:47.057
My mom is gonna be
very upset with us.

12:47.059 --> 12:48.925
"Us"?

12:48.927 --> 12:50.127
You threw the bachelor party.

12:50.129 --> 12:52.429
You hired strippers!

12:52.431 --> 12:54.697
That's why I said "us."

12:54.699 --> 12:56.199
You know what,
it ultimately doesn't matter

12:56.201 --> 12:58.251
because in your mother's eyes.
it's all your fault.

12:58.253 --> 12:59.519
(sighs) You're right.

12:59.521 --> 13:01.588
She has never forgiven me
for her prolapsed vagina.

13:01.590 --> 13:03.757
And I'm never gonna forgive you

13:03.759 --> 13:05.559
for putting that picture
in my head.

13:05.561 --> 13:07.728
It's not my fault my ears
got caught.

13:08.896 --> 13:11.064
She's gonna be crushed,
and it's all because of us.

13:11.066 --> 13:12.432
Will you stop saying that!

13:12.434 --> 13:13.884
It's because of you!

13:13.886 --> 13:18.021
First you destroyed her vagina,
and now it's her dreams.

13:18.023 --> 13:19.272
Really?

13:19.274 --> 13:21.441
I thought, as partners,
we shared the burdens of life

13:21.443 --> 13:22.725
for better or for worse.

13:22.727 --> 13:24.227
Or were they just empty vows?

13:24.229 --> 13:26.363
We're not married!

13:26.365 --> 13:28.949
Oh, you don't have
to remind me of that.

13:29.784 --> 13:32.068
We're not gay!

13:32.070 --> 13:34.588
I can see why we have
to tell other people that,

13:34.590 --> 13:37.090
but we shouldn't have
to tell each other!

13:39.510 --> 13:41.461
Oh, hey, Alan,
look who's here.

13:41.463 --> 13:43.046
Hello, boys.

13:43.048 --> 13:44.247
Hey, you want a drink?

13:44.249 --> 13:45.415
(both laugh)

13:45.417 --> 13:46.749
I know, stupid question.

13:46.751 --> 13:49.419
Hey, Mommy,
did you have fun shopping?

13:49.421 --> 13:50.871
What's wrong?

13:50.873 --> 13:52.389
What-what do you mean,
"what's wrong"?

13:52.391 --> 13:53.974
You're using
that same whiny voice

13:53.976 --> 13:56.560
you used when you pooped
your pants in ballet class.

13:56.562 --> 13:58.478
Good Lord.
I was a kid!

13:58.480 --> 14:00.147
You were 14.

14:01.199 --> 14:02.999
You finally had a bulge
in your tights,

14:03.001 --> 14:04.935
and it was on the wrong side.

14:04.937 --> 14:06.236
Okay, you know, I thought this

14:06.238 --> 14:07.871
was gonna be difficult,
but maybe not.

14:07.873 --> 14:10.040
Marty ran off
with a couple of strippers.

14:10.825 --> 14:12.209
Excuse me?

14:12.211 --> 14:15.662
Things got a little crazy
at the bachelor party.

14:15.664 --> 14:16.746
What happened?

14:16.748 --> 14:17.798
Did he eat sugar?

14:17.800 --> 14:20.634
He may have.

14:22.954 --> 14:24.287
All right.

14:24.289 --> 14:26.306
Well, I guess he's having
one last little fling

14:26.308 --> 14:27.674
before the wedding.

14:27.676 --> 14:30.093
Um, y-yeah, about the wedding.

14:30.095 --> 14:33.563
There's that same
tutu-crapping voice again.

14:34.348 --> 14:36.266
He called it off.

14:36.268 --> 14:38.185
What?

14:38.986 --> 14:40.070
Sorry, Evelyn.

14:40.072 --> 14:41.304
But...

14:41.306 --> 14:43.190
the strippers have
his medication,

14:43.192 --> 14:45.859
and I think one of them has
a nurse's outfit.

14:47.495 --> 14:49.529
You know, I-I think if you went
over there and talked to him,

14:49.531 --> 14:51.198
you might be able
to change his mind.

14:51.200 --> 14:54.150
He may have even forgotten
he called off the wedding.

14:54.152 --> 14:57.504
No, if he doesn't want
to get married, that's fine.

14:58.589 --> 14:59.539
Are you okay?

14:59.541 --> 15:00.841
I mean,
is there anything we can do?

15:00.843 --> 15:02.425
I'm all right.

15:02.427 --> 15:05.095
You can't force someone
to love you.

15:07.465 --> 15:08.998
Excuse me.

15:09.000 --> 15:10.867
(sighs)

15:10.869 --> 15:12.886
What did I miss?

15:12.888 --> 15:14.804
Well, the wedding's off,

15:14.806 --> 15:17.390
and Alan crapped his pants
in ballet class.

15:19.110 --> 15:21.010
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:21.012 --> 15:22.229
Wow.

15:22.231 --> 15:23.530
Yeah.

15:23.532 --> 15:24.698
If I inherit this place,

15:24.700 --> 15:26.900
there's a guest room
with your name on it.

15:28.653 --> 15:30.904
Man, he bought this
with sitcom money.

15:32.573 --> 15:35.575
I am in the wrong business.

15:37.245 --> 15:38.545
May I help you?

15:38.547 --> 15:40.330
Uh, we're here
to see Marty.

15:40.332 --> 15:42.165
I'm sorry, Mr. Pepper is busy.

15:42.167 --> 15:44.534
Really? Uh, he doesn't have time

15:44.536 --> 15:47.220
to visit with Ralph Macchio?

15:47.222 --> 15:49.422
A thousand apologies,
Mr. Macchio.

15:49.424 --> 15:51.091
Right this way.

15:51.093 --> 15:53.593
After you, Daniel-san.

15:53.595 --> 15:55.896
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

15:59.967 --> 16:01.518
We're going to take a bath.

16:01.520 --> 16:04.387
You can start washing
each other.

16:05.306 --> 16:08.158
But save the dirty parts for me.

16:08.993 --> 16:10.327
(knocking)

16:10.329 --> 16:11.695
Who's there?

16:11.697 --> 16:13.363
Uh, it's Alan and Walden.

16:13.365 --> 16:15.732
Who?

16:15.734 --> 16:17.033
(sighs)

16:17.035 --> 16:19.920
Evelyn's gay son
and his boyfriend.

16:19.922 --> 16:21.404
Oh.

16:21.406 --> 16:23.924
All right, come on in.

16:24.759 --> 16:26.876
If you're here
to change my mind,

16:26.878 --> 16:28.428
forget it.

16:28.430 --> 16:30.096
But I-I thought you
loved my mother.

16:30.098 --> 16:31.848
I do,

16:31.850 --> 16:34.884
but I'm not ready
to settle down.

16:34.886 --> 16:37.587
Maybe when I get a little older.

16:37.589 --> 16:41.691
Marty, I don't
say this unkindly,

16:41.693 --> 16:45.645
but if you get any older,
you'll be soil.

16:46.731 --> 16:48.598
Besides, you know
my mother.

16:48.600 --> 16:50.317
She'd sleep with you
and the strippers.

16:50.319 --> 16:51.735
Oh, yeah,
she's a big whore.

16:51.737 --> 16:52.935
Yeah.

16:52.937 --> 16:57.123
I'm not saying
she doesn't have her charms.

16:57.125 --> 16:58.658
So, what's the problem?

16:58.660 --> 16:59.960
The truth is,

16:59.962 --> 17:02.495
I'm a six-time loser
at marriage,

17:02.497 --> 17:05.465
and I don't want to go
for a seventh.

17:06.300 --> 17:07.884
I get it.

17:07.886 --> 17:09.803
You're-you're scared.

17:09.805 --> 17:11.921
But, you know,
in-in love,

17:11.923 --> 17:15.392
you have to take a leap
and hope for the best.

17:15.394 --> 17:17.727
That should be written
on a pillow--

17:17.729 --> 17:20.263
the pillow you can bite
when you and your buddy are...

17:20.265 --> 17:21.314
All right, all right.

17:21.316 --> 17:22.649
Um...

17:25.469 --> 17:29.406
No, all-all I'm saying is
is that marriage

17:29.408 --> 17:31.441
can be a beautiful thing.

17:31.443 --> 17:34.744
So, why aren't you two married?

17:34.746 --> 17:36.363
Yeah.

17:36.365 --> 17:38.081
Why aren't we married, Walden?

17:39.834 --> 17:41.835
This isn't what you think it is.

17:41.837 --> 17:43.086
Right.

17:43.088 --> 17:47.924
I don't understand you,
but you understand me.

17:47.926 --> 17:49.342
You're right.

17:49.344 --> 17:50.343
He's right.

17:50.345 --> 17:51.695
I-I don't want to

17:51.697 --> 17:54.297
end up alone

17:54.299 --> 17:57.484
and a-afraid of commitment
like Marty.

17:59.420 --> 18:01.104
Alan...

18:02.006 --> 18:04.190
...for the last
three years of my life,

18:04.192 --> 18:06.676
you have...

18:06.678 --> 18:08.728
always been there.

18:08.730 --> 18:10.280
Every day.

18:10.282 --> 18:13.700
When I wake up in the morning,
when I go to bed at night,

18:13.702 --> 18:15.368
there you are.

18:17.988 --> 18:19.489
So, nobody is more surprised

18:19.491 --> 18:22.459
to hear this coming
out of my mouth than me.

18:22.461 --> 18:24.694
This is not happening.

18:25.963 --> 18:27.997
Alan Harper...

18:27.999 --> 18:29.699
will you marry me?

18:30.501 --> 18:31.835
Yes! Yes!

18:31.837 --> 18:33.536
A billion times, yes!

18:33.538 --> 18:34.671
Okay, okay.

18:34.673 --> 18:35.958
All right, okay.

18:35.960 --> 18:37.492
Let's save something
for the honeymoon.

18:37.494 --> 18:39.628
Ibiza, it has to be Ibiza.

18:39.630 --> 18:41.046
You're right.

18:41.048 --> 18:44.416
Excluding my heart,
kidney and liver,

18:44.418 --> 18:46.918
I'm not a young man anymore.

18:49.055 --> 18:50.705
I'm gonna call your mother.

18:50.707 --> 18:52.207
SUGAR:
Marty,

18:52.209 --> 18:54.109
come find the ducky.

18:54.111 --> 18:55.394
(giggling)

18:55.396 --> 18:57.846
We-we should probably go
break the news to them.

18:57.848 --> 19:00.899
Yeah, yeah, that'd probably be
the proper thing to do.

19:02.101 --> 19:03.268
Just so you know,

19:03.270 --> 19:05.487
this is not happening
when we're married.

19:05.489 --> 19:07.906
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:15.423 --> 19:17.023
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

19:17.025 --> 19:18.608
Marty,

19:18.610 --> 19:21.360
I love you more than words
could ever say.

19:21.362 --> 19:22.945
From the moment

19:22.947 --> 19:25.281
I took off my blindfold,
turned around

19:25.283 --> 19:28.117
and saw you behind me
for the first time,

19:28.119 --> 19:31.871
I knew I'd never need
a safe word again.

19:32.656 --> 19:35.124
I wish I had
one of those right now.

19:35.126 --> 19:37.326
Which? The blindfold
or the safe word?

19:37.328 --> 19:39.829
Yes.

19:39.831 --> 19:43.466
Evelyn, I'm so happy
you're in my life.

19:43.468 --> 19:46.452
When I'm with you,
I feel like I'm 85 again.

19:46.454 --> 19:48.671
You're the perfect
girl for me.

19:48.673 --> 19:50.339
You make my heart skip a beat,

19:50.341 --> 19:53.626
and you know how to use
a defribrillator.

19:53.628 --> 19:54.961
(laughter)

19:54.963 --> 19:58.130
I wrote that joke.

19:58.132 --> 20:00.650
Last night, I only got up
one time to pee.

20:02.236 --> 20:05.404
I peed a second time,
but I-I didn't get up.

20:08.825 --> 20:11.110
Ashes to ashes,

20:11.112 --> 20:12.478
and dust to dust...

20:12.480 --> 20:14.813
Oh, I'm sorry.
I skipped a page there.

20:14.815 --> 20:16.198
Uh...

20:16.200 --> 20:18.417
you may now kiss the bride.

20:24.908 --> 20:28.160
Congratulations, Evelyn,
on a beautiful ceremony.

20:28.162 --> 20:31.180
Yeah. Can't wait
for the next one.

20:31.949 --> 20:33.349
I just have to tell you,

20:33.351 --> 20:35.668
I am a huge fan.
Thank you very much.

20:35.670 --> 20:38.271
I lost my virginity
to one of your records.

20:38.273 --> 20:41.307
A-side and B-side,
if you know what I mean.

20:41.309 --> 20:42.725
(laughs)

20:42.727 --> 20:45.978
Oh, I just became
a big fan of yours, baby.

20:45.980 --> 20:47.029
(laughs)

20:47.031 --> 20:49.865
And I just want
to say one thing.

20:49.867 --> 20:53.736
None of this would've happened
without these two.

20:53.738 --> 20:55.955
And as my present to you,

20:55.957 --> 20:58.574
I've arranged for Tim

20:58.576 --> 21:02.211
to perform
one more wedding ceremony.

21:02.213 --> 21:05.414
(applause)

21:07.711 --> 21:10.596
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

21:10.598 --> 21:13.594
Oh, my God.
Oh, my God.

